   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "I hope / I would like",
     "texto": [
      "**-(으)면 좋겠어요** expresses that the speaker wants a situation to come true: 날씨가 **좋으면 좋겠어요** (I hope the weather is good), 합격하면 좋겠어요 (I hope to pass). The wish can refer to the speaker or to another person, depending on the context."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Telling condition and wish apart",
     "texto": [
      "**-(으)면** followed by another action sets up a condition: **날씨가 좋으면 공원에 가요** = if the weather is good, we go to the park. **-(으)면 좋겠어요** adds the wish: **날씨가 좋으면 좋겠어요** = I hope the weather is good. To wish for an action you want to do yourself, **-았/었으면 좋겠어요** is also common; for now just recognise it: 한국에 갔으면 좋겠어요 = I hope I can go to Korea."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
